  "notes": "{叩|たた}く means to hit, knock, or beat. A transitive godan verb with both physical and figurative uses.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ドアを{叩|たた}く: to knock on a door\n- {太鼓|たいこ}を{叩|たた}く: to beat a drum\n- {肩|かた}を{叩|たた}く: to pat on the shoulder\n- {手|て}を{叩|たた}く: to clap hands\n- キーボードを{叩|たた}く: to type (lit. hit the keyboard)\n\nFIGURATIVE USE:\n{叩|たた}く can mean \"to criticize harshly\":\n- マスコミに{叩|たた}かれる: to be attacked by media\n- ネットで{叩|たた}かれる: to be criticized online\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive verb. No common intransitive pair.",
